      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Maybe I found the cause. `AvatarDescriptorEditor3` is missing `_repaint = false` in the update loop. So, if once `_repaint` becomes true, it continues to `SetDirty` until quitting the editor. I think it should be false at the beginning of `OnInspectorGUI`.\n\nSimple repro steps:\n\n1. Create a new Scene. Add a GameObject. Add VRCAvatarDescriptor.\n\n2. Save the Scene. Check if the dirty mark disappears.\n\n3. Show VRCAvatarDescriptor in the Inspector. Press the \"Edit\" button in the \"View Position\" property.\n\n4. Then the dirty mark shows up. It continues to be dirty even if you save the Scene.\n\nI checked with SDK version 3.1.11 and 3.1.10.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
